  "body": "## Problem and behavior\n\nFollowing one artist currently copies a fan profile into the club and creates reciprocal follows with every existing member. Retire those implicit profile/relationship writes and new named notifications once canonical enforcement exists, while preserving the directed artist subscription and historical data. Follow/unfollow now share the current-session and ordered account locks; retries preserve the existing DTO and subscription timestamp. Correct the member-profile empty state so missing profile data does not imply absent membership.\n\n**Dependency:** #409, exact parent `7e601607f60b2987e502c4a14db821bbf37df296` (on #402 \u2192 #397 \u2192 #390). Keep draft/unmerged. No deployment or production activation.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Executable TLA+/TLC: 12,738 distinct states, safety/progress passed, four required counterexamples; 708 observed transitions generate real HTTP cases.\n- Private PostgreSQL HTTP: **1,141 examples, zero failures**, including activation/block/closure/token and POST/DELETE races.\n- Stack GHC 9.10.3: **2,542 examples, zero failures**.\n- Native PostgreSQL16.10 complete schema: 102 registered migrations, additive apply/reapply/pause and preserved-write checks passed. Local Docker PG17 failed with a read-only filesystem; hosted PG17 complete-schema checks subsequently passed in the social workflow.\n- UI app TypeScript, changed-page ESLint, existing selector contracts **11/11**, catalog audit passed. No new browser/native journey claimed.\n- Synthetic 100/10,000-member handler p95 **49.22/50.05ms**, below predeclared 100/250ms limits (40 samples). Legacy single probes 298.93ms/>10s. Excludes initial authentication/network; not production capacity evidence.\n\nCommands, raw model/counterexample output, test logs, source fingerprints, failed development runs and acceptance statuses: [review packet](docs/social/fan-effects-boundary.md), [evidence](docs/social/evidence/fan-effects-20260916/). Exact-head [social CI35144567539](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35144567539) passed both model/PostgreSQL and social-client/browser jobs, including complete PG17 schema qualification. [Full CI35144567540](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35144567540) has passed UI, persona browser, migration/production-migration, repository and API-contract jobs; backend build/test is still running. Do not count pending or skipped jobs as passed. Later evidence is recorded in #394 without restarting this implementation run.\n\n## Migration, flags and rollback\n\nApply `tdf-hq/sql/2026-09-16_social_v2_fan_effects.sql` after dependencies: one function, no new tables/indexes/backfill or automatic production migration registration. Preserve the existing inactive flags and durable activation latch. Drain old follow/unfollow writers before enforcement; mixed writers are not qualified. Missing adapters fail closed.\n\nPause keeps the latch/adapter and all new subscriptions/engagement records. Do not restore unsafe old writers or reset activation memory; disable these routes if the boundary cannot be retained. No historical profile, relationship or notification deletion.\n\n## Remaining limits\n\nHistorical notification serving/counts lack follower provenance; artist-follow GET, explicit member-profile publication/privacy and actor-scoped caches still block rollout. Role-grant races, managed-entity delegation, spam qualification, full browser/native journeys and earlier integration gaps remain open. No production conversion gain claimed. The prior automatic provider-deployment exception remains documented for owner review; this branch uses provider-skip protections.\n",
